hexagon: state the L2 limit of the dirty range tracker
Fold-into: upstream/hexagon-host

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The dirty range tracker of the DSP writes back and invalidates the lines of
a range with hex_l2flush, a dccleaninva loop. On the v79 that loop does not
reach the lines of the L2 cache, and the DMA transfers of the kernels
bypass L2. Thus inside one op batch, an op can read an old line of L2
after a DMA write, or the write-back of an old line can go over the bytes
of a DMA write. The full write-back and invalidate at the start and at the
end of each batch reaches L2, thus a batch of one op cannot have this
property.

This patch states that limit in a comment of htp-tensor.c. The code does
not change. A range call of qurt_mem_cache_clean for each op, or DMA
transfers through L2, close the property, but they cost decode or prefill
time.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/htp-tensor.c b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/htp-tensor.c
index 760ccd8..7a90a2b 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/htp-tensor.c
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/htp-tensor.c
@@ -11,6 +11,13 @@
 #include "htp-ctx.h"
 #include "work-queue.h"
 
+// The tracker writes back and invalidates the lines of a range with hex_l2flush, a dccleaninva loop.
+// On the v79 that loop does not reach the lines of the L2 cache, and the DMA transfers of the kernels
+// bypass L2. Thus inside one op batch, a line of L2 can hold old bytes of a range that a DMA transfer
+// wrote, or dirty bytes that a DMA transfer does not read. The full write-back and invalidate at the
+// start and at the end of each batch (qurt_mem_cache_clean) reaches L2. A range call of
+// qurt_mem_cache_clean for each op also reaches L2, but it costs decode and prefill time.
+
 struct l2flush_range {
     uint32_t start;       // line-aligned start address
     uint32_t end;         // line-aligned end address
